      "text": "Bogotá’s Historic Centre and Monserrate"
    },
    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:4b5ff9b4a37f43cc",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "4bfc905a8a2c85493b57ed6934141ee3d90251a3e584bab4160ad21466655d1a",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-20261109-f7d28995258f43d8b02d73d0103556dd",
        "model": "GPT-6.1"
      },
      "text": "After breakfast, you’ll meet your English-speaking guide and set out on a tour of Bogotá’s historic centre.\n\nYou’ll walk through old neighbourhoods with colonial churches, narrow streets, historic squares and monuments from the 17th to the 19th centuries. Next to the old part of the city are modern districts with high-rise buildings, cafés, restaurants and shops.\n\nThe tour includes the Gold Museum, which houses a large collection of pre-Columbian objects: gold masks, diadems, bracelets, ritual figurines and symbols of authority. Gold held special symbolic meaning for ancient cultures, which associated it with the energy of the sun.\n\nThen take the funicular up Monserrate. The hill rises to about 3,200 metres above sea level, and the viewpoints near the top offer a panorama of Bogotá. The 17th-century San Vicente Monastery stands at the summit.\n\nNext, visit the Fernando Botero Museum. After the museum, have lunch at a restaurant, then return to your hotel to rest."
    },
